{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1527075-wod-20th-edition-crossover-discord-server-recruiting","id":1527075,"title":"WoD 20th Edition crossover Discord server - recruiting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-18T17:57:02-08:00","id":1527075,"title":"WoD 20th Edition crossover Discord server - recruiting","content":"Sleepless in Seattle is a play-by-post living world/ 24/7 Discord server that's been running for a few years now, and we use the 20th Anniversary edition of World of Darkness (+ some older-edition compilations). We support WtA, VtM, CtD, and MtA. Sorcerers are now available for MtA, and currently capped for WtA. The server is set in Seattle and surrounding areas, in rough keeping with current date but not recent events such as COVID. Each venue usually focuses on plots within the splat, but at times may participate in certain cross-splat plots.<br /> <br /> <u><b>At the moment, we are prioritizing looking for assistant Storytellers for the WtA, CtD, and MtA venues</b></u> - specifically a Technocrat ST for the latter. You do not need to have experience with any splat other than your own, and timezones can be flexible. Details for what we are looking for in an assistant ST will vary, but in general, we would like them to help come up with and run plots, as well as play NPCs where necessary to give players some interaction and direction. STs can still have their own characters too. Please let me know if there are questions, and I'll either answer them (I am the WtA main ST) or point you towards the appropriate ST via Discord DM. If you are looking to be a player, please be aware that because we're searching for STs, some splats may close to new characters, or you may mostly be socializing with other players before getting the chance to go on plots.<br /> <br /> Here are quick descriptions for each of the venues' settings and/or running plots:<br /> <b>CtD:</b> (Seelie/Unseelie + some Thallain) The Duchy of the Emerald City is lively with political secrets the locals have yet to uncover. The mysterious Duke Caspian Militiades has made a variety of lenient rulings toward the local Thallain, making him a hot topic with the nobility. But after he returned from his absence of many months, some nobles wonder if he's fit to keep his title...<br /> <br /> <b>MtA:</b> (Tradition/Disparate/Techie) In the twilight of the Ascension War, the various sects are in an uneasy ceasefire. And yet on the edge of reality, from the fringes of Horizon, to the darkest alley of Seattle, something new is approaching. Time and space is unraveling, worlds and places that never were or could be are leaking in, bringing with them familiar faces and strange terrors. But neither the Traditionalists, the Technocrats, or Disparates are prepared for what's truly coming.<br /> <br /> <b>VtM:</b> (Camarilla clans + select bloodlines) The vampires of Seattle are still recovering from a Sabbat invasion, only just rebuffed on the myriad battlefields of conflict, finance, politics and corruption. Others finally are able to take time for more personal quests, although they may not always like the answers. The Tremere work to improve their image after the revelation that their former Primogen had been making Gargoyles for some time - who now have the uncommon honor of a seat on the Primogen Council, in no small thanks to the Nosferatu. Despite all this positivity, the Prince has been cloistered away for months now, allowing her Seneschal to represent her in Elysiums. What keeps her busy? What does this mean for the city? And why does the city seem a little darker each night...<br /> <br /> <b>WtA:</b> (Fera + Samsa homebrew) After recently having been accepted, after many trials, as the first Ahadi sept in America, the mixed-Fera sept of Past's Renewal is still vigilant for new threats. The Wyrm has gotten creative with its Mockery Breeds in the past, and continually seeks out new and vile ways to twist what Gaia has made to its own ends. The Changing Breeds hope to learn from the times long-ago, with the wars, the triumphs, and the fallen, but so too can the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Server link: <a href=\"https://discord.gg/e6XtY979Zd\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/e6XtY979Zd</a><br /> <br /> February update: we've found a couple of VtM STs, but are now looking for a CtD ST instead. CtD is close to closing for players, but remains open for the moment.<br /> <br /> July update: WtA, MtA and CtD are now closed, due to more player interest than incoming STs. Vamp is still open, but we are prioritizing getting STs only now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka","user":"Dehaka","date":". 07-30-2024, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka","name":"Dehaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28297_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}